add(R, `다음 <보기>의 ⓐ~ⓖ 중, 어법상 어색한 문장을 두 개 골라 그 기호를 쓰고, 어색한 부분을 한 군데씩 고쳐 전체를 다시 쓰시오.${FULL}\n\n<보기>\nⓐ I can't understand what she said.\nⓑ What you need is a good long holiday.\nⓒ I have to do that my mom told me to do.\nⓓ I found the key that I have lost in the park.\nⓔ Mr. Kim is the only man that came to the party.\nⓕ He told me that he had never seen a parrot before.\nⓖ When I called his office, he had already gone to the bank.\n\n(1) 기호: ____ → 고친 문장: ______________________\n(2) 기호: ____ → 고친 문장: ______________________`, 'ⓒ → I have to do what my mom told me to do. / ⓓ → I found the key that I had lost in the park.', null, { subParts: [{ label: '(1)', answer: 'ⓒ → I have to do what my mom told me to do.', acceptedAnswers: ['ⓒ, I have to do what my mom told me to do.'] }, { label: '(2)', answer: 'ⓓ → I found the key that I had lost in the park.', acceptedAnswers: ['ⓓ → I found the key that I lost in the park.', 'ⓓ, I found the key that I had lost in the park.'] }] });
add(R, `다음 우리말과 같은 뜻이 되도록 빈칸에 들어갈 말을 주어진 <조건>에 알맞게 완성하시오.\n\n(1) 이것이 내가 사야 하는 것이다.\n(2) 우리는 Sue가 우리를 위해 요리해준 것을 먹었다.\n(3) 나는 내가 주문했던 것을 아직 못 받았다.\n\n<조건>\n• (1), (2), (3) 모두 관계대명사 what을 사용할 것\n• <보기>의 단어 및 표현을 사용할 것 (필요시 변형할 것)\n• 각 빈칸에 한 단어씩 쓸 것\n\n<보기> for, buy, cook, order, have to\n\n(1) This is ____ ____ ____ ____ ____.\n(2) We ate ____ ____ ____ ____ ____ ____.\n(3) I haven't get ____ ____ ____.`, 'what I have to buy / what Sue had cooked for us / what I ordered', null, { subParts: [{ label: '(1)', answer: 'what I have to buy' }, { label: '(2)', answer: 'what Sue had cooked for us', acceptedAnswers: ['what Sue cooked for us'] }, { label: '(3)', answer: 'what I ordered', acceptedAnswers: ['what I had ordered'] }] });
